{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Buy us and our farmland</b> — behold, they said to him that he should buy even their persons as slaves to Pharaoh, and so he said, \"See, I have acquired you this day and your farmland.\" But he said, \"Joseph acquired all the farmland of Egypt for Pharaoh, for the Egyptians sold each his field,\" and he did not say that he acquired their persons, only the land. And the reason is that they said to him to buy them as slaves to do the king's labor at his pleasure, but he did not wish to buy anything except the land, and he stipulated with them that they would work it forever and be upon it tenant farmers of the ancestral houses for Pharaoh. And afterward he said to them, \"See, I have acquired you this day and your farmland for Pharaoh\" — not as slaves as you said to me, but rather together with the land you shall be his. Now it is fitting that the king, who is the lord of the soil, should take four-fifths and you the fifth, but I will deal kindly with you: you shall take the portion of the owner of the soil and Pharaoh shall take the portion fitting for the tenant farmer, but you shall be acquired by him so that you cannot leave the fields. And this is the reason for what they vowed to him: \"and as for the land, it shall not be sold\" — that it not be sold forever. Therefore they said to him, \"We have found favor in the eyes of my lord,\" for you have lightened our burden by taking four-fifths with which we can live, \"and we shall be slaves to Pharaoh\" as we vowed — to work the land at his pleasure:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {0 "Reading ארבע הידות as 'four-fifths,' following Ramban's interpretation of the grain-sharing arrangement; the literal sense 'four hands' functions here as a fraction idiom."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:46:08.656783292Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}